      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The effects of low-intensive tractions were evaluated clinically and electrophysiologically in 148 patients with neurological symptoms of lumbar osteochondrosis. The above tractions were combined with vibration, peloid electrophoresis and sulphide baths. Indications and contraindications for tractions are outlined. The above complexes are recommended for use in the programs of rehabilitation of patients with osteochondrosis of the lumbar spine."},
